From: waydroid contributors
Subject: [PATCH 0007] experimental rootless mode

Per-user fuse mounts and an idmapped, unprivileged LXC container, with the
container mounting its own binderfs.  Applied after the rebrand because it
edits the rebranded code and adds tools/helpers/rootless.py and
data/configs/waydroid-binder.rc.

diff --git a/data/configs/waydroid-binder.rc b/data/configs/waydroid-binder.rc
--- a/data/configs/waydroid-binder.rc	1970-01-01 10:00:00.000000000 +1000
+++ b/data/configs/waydroid-binder.rc	2026-10-06 16:18:35.472754666 +1100
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Waydroid: bring up the binder devices inside the container.
+#
+# A user namespace may mount binderfs, so nothing on the host has to provide
+# /dev/binder, /dev/vndbinder or /dev/hwbinder for a rootless container: the
+# container's own root mounts them and binderfs creates the nodes from the
+# kernel's ANDROID_BINDER_DEVICES list (which the NixOS module pins to
+# binder,vndbinder,hwbinder).  This is also why rootless Waydroid needs no root
+# helper, no dedicated group and no device nodes on the host.
+#
+# Android's first-stage init would normally mount binderfs itself, but rootless
+# mode skips that stage (device mknod is refused in a user namespace), so it
+# happens from here instead.
+on early-init
+    mkdir /dev/binderfs 0755 root root
+    exec - root root -- /system/bin/mount -t binder binder /dev/binderfs
+    symlink /dev/binderfs/binder /dev/binder
+    symlink /dev/binderfs/vndbinder /dev/vndbinder
+    symlink /dev/binderfs/hwbinder /dev/hwbinder
